–210. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Trecca EMC, Gelardi M, Cassano M. COVID-19 and hearing difficulties. Am J Otolaryngol 2020; 41(4): 102496. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Sriwijitalai W, Wiwanitkit V. Hearing loss and COVID-19: a note. Am J Otolaryngol 2020; 41(3): 102473. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Karimi-Galougahi M, Naeini AS, Raad N, et al. Vertigo and hearing loss during the COVID-19 pandemic – is there an association? Acta Otorhinolaryngol Ital 2020; 40(6): 463–465. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Chen X, Fu YY, Zhang TY. Role of viral infection in sudden hearing loss. J Int Med Res 2019; 47(7): 2865–2872. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Gelardi M, Iannuzzi L, Trecca EMC, et al. COVID-19: what happened to all of the otolaryngology emergencies? Eur Arch Otorhinolaryngol 2020; 277(11): 3231–3232. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Di Saverio S, Khan M, Pata F, et al. Laparoscopy at all costs? Not now during COVID-19 outbreak and not for acute care surgery and emergency colorectal surgery: a practical algorithm from a hub tertiary teaching hospital in Northern Lombardy, Italy. J Trauma Acute Care Surg 2020; 88(6): 715–718. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Ielpo B, Podda M, Pellino G, et al. Global attitudes in the management of acute appendicitis during COVID-19 pandemic: ACIE Appy Study. Br J Surg. Epub ahead of print 8October2020. DOI: 10.1002/bjs.11999. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 31. Di Saverio S, Pata F, Gallo G, et al. Coronavirus pandemic and colorectal surgery: practical advice based on the Italian experience. Colorectal Dis 2020; 22(6): 625–634. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Yánez Benítez C, Ribeiro MAF, Alexandrino H, et al. International cooperation group of emergency surgery during the COVID-19 pandemic. Eur J