siology. 2008;108(5):812–821. doi: 10.1097/ALN.0b013e31816d83e4. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Wang YP, Gorenstein C. Assessment of depression in medical patients: a systematic review of the utility of the Beck depression inventory-II. Clinics (Sao Paulo) 2013;68(9):1274–1287. doi: 10.6061/clinics/2013(09)15. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Larrosa F, Roura J, Dura MJ, Guirao M, Alberti A, Alobid I. Adaptation and validation of the Spanish version of the nasal obstruction symptom evaluation (NOSE) scale. Rhinology. 2015;53(2):176–180. doi: 10.4193/Rhin14.137. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Flemons WW. Clinical practice. Obstructive sleep apnea. N Engl J Med. 2002;347(7):498–504. doi: 10.1056/NEJMcp012849. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Qaseem A, Dallas P, Owens DK, Starkey M, Holty JE, Shekelle P, et al. Diagnosis of obstructive sleep apnea in adults: a clinical practice guideline from theAmerican College of Physicians. Ann Intern Med. 2014;161(3):210–220. doi: 10.7326/M12-3187. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Kapur VK, Auckley DH, Chowdhuri S, Kuhlmann DC, Mehra R, Ramar K, et al. Clinical practice guideline for diagnostic testing for adult obstructive sleep apnea: an American Academy of sleep medicine clinical practice guideline. J Clin Sleep Med. 2017;13(3):479–504. doi: 10.5664/jcsm.6506. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Saldías F, Gassmann J, Canelo A, Uribe J, Díaz Patiño O. Accuracy of sleep questionnaires for obstructive sleep apnea syndrome screening. Rev Med Chile 2018; 146: 1123–1134. 2018;146:1123–34. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 23. Jorquera J, Freire M, Munoz P, F S. Utilidad de los indices clinicos y oximetricos en el diagnostico de apnea obstructiva del sueno moderada a severa. XXXV Congreso Chileno de Enfermedades Respiratorias; Valdivia: Rev. Chil. Enferm respir.; 2002. 24. Corral J, Sanchez-Quiroga MA, Carmona-Bernal C, Sanchez-Armengol A, Sanchez-de-la-