erature review, and proposed mitigation strategies. Int Forum Allergy Rhinol. 2020;10(7):798-805. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 13. Zayas G, Dimitry J, Zayas A, O’Brien D, King M. A new paradigm in respiratory hygiene: increasing the cohesivity of airway secretions to improve cough interaction and reduce aerosol dispersion. BMC Pulm Med. 2005;5:1-12. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 14. Chen JX, Workman AD, Chari DA, et al. Demonstration and mitigation of aerosol and particle dispersion during mastoidectomy relevant to the COVID-19 era. Otol Neurotol. 2020;41(9):1230-1239. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 15. Vukkadala N, Qian ZJ, Holsinger FC, Patel ZM, Rosenthal E. COVID-19 and the otolaryngologist: preliminary evidence-based review. Laryngoscope. 2020;130(11):2537-2543. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 16. Singhal T. A review of coronavirus disease-2019 (COVID-19). Indian J Pediatr. 2020;87(4):281-286. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Rothe C, Schunk M, Sothmann P, et al. Transmission of 2019-NCOV infection from an asymptomatic contact in Germany. N Engl J Med. 2020;382(10):970-971. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Vlantis AC, Tsang RKY, Wong DKK, Woo JKS, Van Hasselt CA. The impact of severe acute respiratory syndrome on otorhinolaryngological services at the Prince of Wales Hospital in Hong Kong. Laryngoscope. 2004;114(1):171-174. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Hollander JE, Carr BG. Virtually perfect? Telemedicine for Covid-19. N Engl J Med. 2020;382(18):1679-1681. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Kane CK, Gillis K. The use of telemedicine by physicians: still the exception rather than the rule. Health Aff. 2018;37(12):1923-1930. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Sohn GK, Wong DJ, Yu SS. A review of the use of telemedicine in dermatologic surgery. Dermatol Surg. 2020;46(4):501-507. [ DOI ]